From c6857f3de4a4a8e18d9f5329b53d47eb42c29636 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iskra <iskra@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:53:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Iskra: AMD-Vi IOMMU and PCI device passthrough for vmm
 guests (hypervisor step 8)

A VM can be given a host PCI device through /scheme/sys/vmm: ASSIGN points
the device at a 4-level AMD-Vi I/O page table that maps guest-physical
addresses to the VM's frames (the IOMMU starts lazily; every other device
keeps an invalid DTE, i.e. untranslated DMA), PORTS opens one of its I/O BARs
in the I/O permission map, MMIO maps a memory BAR into the nested page table
uncached at its host address, and DEVCFG proxies its PCI config space.
The device table entry is cleared before the VM's frames are freed.
